{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Let her not be, please, like a dead one.</b> A metzora is accounted as dead. He explained <b>let her not be, please</b> — let not our sister be with slackness in your prayer, like one who emerges a metzora from his mother's womb, and he is immediately as though half his flesh were consumed, as they said: an infant who emerges a metzora from his mother's womb has no purification ever. And since this affliction came by sin, there is an opening to say that through prayer it will depart, as we find with Pharaoh and in other places; therefore you must pray for her. Here Rashi explained: 'and this is כאשר בצאתו מרחם אמו' — meaning, she emerged from our mother's womb, and I cannot purify her, for she is my relative."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:41.811107870Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}